<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chandrayaan-3</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2023">2023</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chandrayaan-3 was a lunar mission of the Indian Space Research Organisation launched in July 2023. On 23 August 2023 its lander Vikram touched down near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhu">Moon</a>'s south pole, the first landing in that region, making <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> the fourth country to achieve a soft landing on the Moon. Its rover Pragyan then studied the lunar surface for about two weeks.</p></div>
